  bootwright / machine
      Manage machine

  Usage
    bootwright machine [flags]

  Commands
  ○ Command | exec
      PURPOSE  Run a command over SSH as the Machine's resolved identity; confirm or refuse an
               unproved host key and return the client's exit status

  ○ Command | info
      PURPOSE  Inspect machine placement, access, and recorded evidence

  ○ Command | list
      PURPOSE  List machines and the lifecycle position each has reached

  ○ Command | restart
      PURPOSE  Restart machines through their management controllers

  ○ Command | rsh
      PURPOSE  Open an SSH session as the Machine's resolved identity; confirm or refuse an
               unproved host key and return the client's exit status

  ○ Command | start
      PURPOSE  Power machines on through their management controllers

  ○ Command | stop
      PURPOSE  Shut machines down through their management controllers

  ○ Command | trust
      PURPOSE  Inspect and maintain exact host-key trust

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.
